ple  part of the country was already occupied  but ukraine was not threatening anyone  and was not attacking  anyone  then came february 24th and a russian  attack  europe changed  i think i am not the only one who would  wake up every night since that day to  see whether kiev  is still standing and it's independent  at the beginning many of us didn't  believe  that it could become reality  kiev  thanks to president zelinski's  leadership  has defended itself  and most of ukraine as well  vladimir zelensky  dennis mihal and their team gave people  courage  and they will to fight every day  when i arrived in kiev on march the 15th  together with prime ministers of poland  and slovenia  at that time there was  still  a curfew checkpoints and roadblocks  everywhere  then i understood the reason  why the city had not fallen  every ukrainian i met  showed determination and the will to  fight for their freedom  this only reinforced my beliefs that we  must not leave ukraine without help  my country czech republic started  supplying arms to ukraine even before  the war we continue to do so today and  we will continue to supply them in the  next weeks and months  on the territory of our country three  hundred and seventy thousand ukrainian  women children and elderly have found  refuge  more than three and a half percent of  our population  on july the 1st the czech republic took  over the presidency of the council of  the european union  the original priorities we had a few  months ago  are now significantly changed we had to  respond to the war  so a support for ukraine its post-war  reconstruction  and also managing the refugee wave  became the number one priority  these three aspects are closely linked  in order to rebuild we must help ukraine  to defend itself we must continue  supplying arms humanitarian aid but also  money for day-to-day  operations  in order for ukraine to defend itself  its defender must be sure that their  women and children are safe  that is why 